  "arm_notes": {
    "periodic_residual_counts": "EXP-P32/P34/P35 arm unchanged (frozen PLR-lite embedding + residual backbone, blocks Dropout .1, counts workload), old code path; keeps its embed_residual flag, so the robust-clip family predicate is tested first in the runner and scorer",
    "pitcher_id_periodic_residual_counts": "Reference entry + pitcher_id block (direct_pitcher_id_model): TRAIN-only vocabulary of pitcher ids with >= 100 TRAIN rows (sorted), UNK 0 otherwise (rare TRAIN pitchers and ids first seen after TRAIN), index appended as the last context column and stripped before the frozen maps; z += P @ T[idx] (T zeros [n_vocab + 1, 8], P [128, 8] private generator seed + 7919) so the untrained network equals the reference at the same seed (P38 entry verbatim)",
    "pitcher_id_row_shuffle_periodic_residual_counts": "Candidate network, parameters and compute; before the vocabulary lookup the split's `pitcher` column is permuted across rows by np.random.default_rng([40001, split position]) (fixed, independent of labels, features and the model seed). Index frequencies and UNK shares are unchanged; the row -> pitcher association is destroyed (information-free).",
    "pitcher_id_dropout_periodic_residual_counts": "Candidate + ID dropout: in training mode each row's index is replaced by UNK with probability 0.2 (private device generator seeded id_seed + 4040; global RNG untouched); eval / calibration / prediction use the true index. Fixed, not tuned.",
    "epoch_cap": "Epoch cap 60, patience 5 for both arms (as EXP-P34-P37). fit.json records cap, epochs_run, best_epoch and stopped_by per fit",
    "parameters": "Reference 244898; the three id arms reference + (n_vocab + 1) x 8 + 128 x 8 (equal among them; n_vocab measured from TRAIN, recorded per fit, checked by the scorer)",
    "capacity": "Candidate vs row-shuffle is parameter- and compute-matched with information removed. The control matches the id path, not a generic wider backbone; a learned per-row noise index is the closest information-free use of the same parameters."
  },
